#import "/modern-iaf/manuals/layout/manual.typ": *

#idx("Instructor")In a #term("lesson") an instructor flies with you and tells you what comes next. You fly the jet. In the F-16D Barak and the F-16I Sufa the instructor sits in the back seat and talks on the intercom: it is always on, with no key clicks. In the F-35I Adir the instructor flies a second F-35I and talks on the radio.

=== The calls <instructor-calls>

#idx("Instructor, calls")A call names the next task at the level of the checklist, for example "Follow the checklist to start the engine". It names the task; its switches are in the checklist. A call comes when you have finished the step before it, and it may be several lines long. Each line shows as a subtitle in the game's language while the instructor says it; the voice is English.

- The first lessons name every step. Later lessons name only what changes.
- Once you have passed every lesson of phase 1, the start-up is yours alone.
- The instructor keeps every comment on your flying for the #term("debrief"). In danger, only the jet's own warnings speak.
- In a check ride the instructor is silent in flight.
- After the flight, the instructor's conclusions are written on the debrief page.
